148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Prior to Section 1033, the US market remained largely untouched by open banking regulations similar to those seen in other regions, such as Europe, Australia and Brazil. However, American consumers have been sharing their financial data with third-party providers since the nineties. Data sharing and service initiation currently exist through custom integrations, proprietary account aggregators and screen scraping. The Section 1033 ruling aims to bolster and regulate these market-driven efforts as they move towards common shared standards for the secure exchange of user-permissioned data, in part by mandating consistent data sharing for financial services providers across the industry.)
/E (Prior to Section 1033, the US market remained largely untouched by open banking regulations similar to those seen in other regions, such as Europe, Australia and Brazil. However, American consumers have been sharing their financial data with third-party providers since the nineties. Data sharing and service initiation currently exist through custom integrations, proprietary account aggregators and screen scraping. The Section 1033 ruling aims to bolster and regulate these market-driven efforts as they move towards common shared standards for the secure exchange of user-permissioned data, in part by mandating consistent data sharing for financial services providers across the industry.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
