/T (Only one standards-setting body that represents a fully-fledged API technical standard has applied for recognition to the CFPB: The Financial Data Exchange, a private, non-profit commonly known as FDX. Since its inception in 2018, FDX and its members have been creating and developing open standards which underpin how open finance currently operates in the US market. As of 2024, the FDX API is used to share over 94 million consumer records, roughly 75% of the addressable market, so it is inevitable that FDX will have a key role in facilitating the US )
