/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Agreement on the high-level technical model for communicating through APIs provides the means for establishing how Data Recipients and Data Providers can communicate securely, using a commonly agreed-upon trust framework. Third-party access has traditionally been enabled like any other API, namely through bi-lateral agreements between Data Recipients, Data Providers and any Data Aggregators. The benefit of a common trust framework is that bi-direction, proprietary trust mechanism can be largely replaced by a more scalable, consistent and secure alternative.  )
/E (Agreement on the high-level technical model for communicating through APIs provides the means for establishing how Data Recipients and Data Providers can communicate securely, using a commonly agreed-upon trust framework. Third-party access has traditionally been enabled like any other API, namely through bi-lateral agreements between Data Recipients, Data Providers and any Data Aggregators. The benefit of a common trust framework is that bi-direction, proprietary trust mechanism can be largely replaced by a more scalable, consistent and secure alternative.  )
